N. J. McCoy wrote:
> I recently had an egg I was carrying around hatch into a pet
> cockatrice.  It seems like it would be a pretty good pet, though I am
> worried about any downsides.  Will it turn feral or turn me into stone
> somehow?

The problem with having a cockatrice as a pet is simply that it isn't
very good.  For all their danger, cockatrices don't have many hit dice,
and pets don't attack monsters more than one hit die above its own
level.  Enemy monsters don't attack pets unless the pet attacks them
first.

Even if you used conflict, the cockatrice's low hit points will mean
that it'll be perishing in short order.

